  "body": "Closes #76\nClaim: ext/bybifok-opus-1\nAuthor model: Opus 5.5\n\n**Problem.** SwiftHFR could not report a message to the moderators. Legacy could, but:\n- it showed any answer from HFR as a success;\n- the Objective-C app removed emoji from the reason without saying so;\n- the Swift service posted to a default address when it could not read the form's action.\n\n**Cause.** LOT-050 had not been written. Its dependencies are merged: LOT-036 (alert form parser), LOT-037 (`.alertPrepare`), LOT-031 (the alert link) and LOT-048 (write conventions).\n\n**Change** (spec `docs/lots/LOT-050-moderator-alert.md`):\n- **`ModeratorAlertFlow.prepare(link:in:)`** (new `HFRClient/Alert/`). It does one GET of the message's alert link through the account's session.\n  - The link is checked first: `https` forum page, path exactly `/user/modo.php`, a single forum `cat`, `post` and `numreponse`.\n  - LOT-037's `.alertPrepare` reading comes first: \"already alerted\" carries HFR's own sentence, never a fixed text (#135 pending).\n  - Otherwise the page must hold the LOT-036 form with `raison`, a non-empty `hash_check` (recorded in the session) and an action that names **the same message** on the forum origin.\n- **`submit(reason:with:)`**:\n  - a blank reason, or one with characters outside the BMP, is refused before sending (Q-3, as for posts);\n  - the form is posted in document order with CRLF, once, redirects not followed, never retried;\n  - HFR's answer is not captured (#136), so every answer with a sentence comes back as `ModeratorAlertAnswer(message:)`, neither a success nor a refusal. Only `W17c`'s logged-out sentence is read. No sentence, or a failed exchange, is `unconfirmed`.\n- **Shared code**: `PostingBody` takes a named textarea (defaults unchanged for posts), and the reason's character check is LOT-096's `PostCharacterCheck.truncatingCharacters(in:)`, the one posts use. HFRParsing gains `HopFormParser.moderationLayout`.\n- **Tests**: `R46`'s prepared form and its POST equal the LOT-004 oracle. `R21`'s link is `R46`'s request. Captured `.hop` pages stand in for the uncaptured shapes. 12 mutations are each caught by a test.\n- No HFRModels type is added or changed. Docs: CHANGELOG-LEGACY row 54 (52 is #363's, 53 is #352's), HFR-PROTOCOL §6c `### LOT-050`.\n\nState-changing flow (a write to HFR): besides the Fable review, it needs a review by another contributor.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
