   "body": "**Adversarial review (Claude Fable 5.1, ext/bybifok-fable-review-9, independent of the author): APPROVE** — head 6b62bd2e\n\nNo security finding: the POST goes only to an action that parses to the same `ModeratorAlertTarget` as the link (https, `forum.hardware.fr`, 443, no user info, exact `/user/modo.php`), `.doNotFollow`, sent once, never retried, 4xx/5xx thrown before parsing; the GET's final URL is re-checked with `isForumPage`; no error carries the reason, token or cookie; nothing is called a success (#136).\n\n1. **Low** — `ModeratorAlertFlow.swift:87`: the #308 compare-and-set is claimed by the spec (Behaviour §2) but untested here. Mutation `updateHashCheck(token)` (no `since:`) passes all 18 alert tests. Fix: a test like the concurrent-login suite using `ScriptedPostingSession.adoptLoginDuringNextRequest`, expecting `hashChecks.isEmpty` and the login's token kept.\n2. **Low** — `ModeratorAlertTarget.swift:41`: `number > 0` → `>= 0` survives; `post=0` / `numreponse=0` links are never tried. Fix: add both to `refusedLinks` (`ModeratorAlertPrepareTests.swift:125`).\n3. **Low** — `ModeratorAlertTarget.swift:18`: the exact-path rule survives `hasSuffix(\"modo.php\")`; no link or action at another path on the forum host (`/modo.php`, `/x/user/modo.php`) is tested. Fix: one such case in `refusedLinks` and in `otherAction`.\n4. **Nit** — `ModeratorAlertFlow.swift:47`: the generic `catch` (\"body\") is unreachable, `PostingBody.make` only throws `.unsupportedForm`; `:125` `tokenField` has no doc line.\n\n**Checked**\n- `swift build --build-tests` then `swift test --skip-build`: 5 targets, 1 222 tests green; no warnings in touched files.\n- 12 mutations: 9 caught (other message's action, redirect followed, logged-out answer, `cat=0`, off-forum redirect, transport→`network`, empty answer, `.write` context, repeated param); 3 survived (above).\n- Captures/oracles: `R21` link = `R46` request; form inputs, `formSubmit` and POST pairs equal `R46.oracle.json`; `R46.meta` (200, no redirect, `md_user`/`md_passs`) backs the HFR-PROTOCOL §6c row; fragments only feed form rules.\n- Legacy `file:line` at `2440d79` all verified (`:154-160`, `:164-176`, `:209`, `:210`, `:229-236`; `ReplyService.swift:1447`, `:1455`, `:1468-1471`, `:1495-1499`).\n- Boundaries: `check-lot-deps.py` 0 violations; Swift 6 Sendable/typed throws; SwiftLint traps (≤140, `id` excluded, complexity ≤9, inclusive language) clean.\n- `Closes #76` open lot issue; `Claim: ext/bybifok-opus-1` equals the issue's `/claim`; CHANGELOG row 51 (50 taken on two other branches); LESSONS 1-55 reviewed.\n\nScratch worktree removed; nothing posted.\n",
