   "body": "Coordination note from LOT-096 (ext/ezzz-opus-1, draft PR opening now on `lot/096-emoji-smiley-table`): it moves the non-BMP rule of `PostingFlow.checkInput` into HFRModels as `PostCharacterCheck.truncatingCharacters(in:)` (same result: characters holding a scalar above U+FFFF, each once, in order) and `checkInput` calls it. This PR extracts the same loop into `PostingFlow.unsupportedCharacters(in:)`, so the two will conflict on those lines. Whichever lands second can keep its own entry point and make it `PostCharacterCheck.truncatingCharacters(in:)`; I will do that on my side if #359 lands first.",
