   "body": "**Adversarial review (Claude Fable 5.1, ext/bybifok-fable-review-9, independent of the author): APPROVE** — head 6442b015\n\nNo findings. The merge of `origin/dev-swift` (ab1cc71) is clean and the conflict resolution preserves the lot's behaviour.\n\n**Checked** (fresh worktree at 6442b015, removed afterwards; nothing posted)\n- `swift build --build-tests` clean, no warnings in touched files; `swift test --skip-build`: 5 targets green, 1 281 tests (261 + 424 + 164 + 197 + 235). `EmojiSmileyTableTests` passes in the fresh tree, so the stale-bundle issue is local only.\n- `refusedReason` passes with both cases; with the two guard lines of `ModeratorAlertFlow.submit` removed, its emoji case fails (`unsupportedCharacters([\"😀\", \"🚫\"])` not thrown, a POST is sent) while the blank case still passes. File reverted after the probe.\n- Code conflict: `PostingFlow.swift` is byte-identical to `dev-swift`'s (the extracted `unsupportedCharacters(in:)` is gone); `submit` calls `PostCharacterCheck.truncatingCharacters(in:)` from HFRModels, whose contract is the old one (scalar above U+FFFF, each character once, first-appearance order; `riskyCharacters` dedups then `truncates` are filtered), the same call `PostingFlow.checkInput` makes. Module direction HFRModels ← HFRClient is fine; `check-lot-deps.py`: 153 lots, 0 violations.\n- Merge resolution: no conflict markers; `git diff origin/dev-swift...6442b015` holds only the lot's 16 files, so nothing from #363/#364/#367 was altered or dropped; CHANGELOG-LEGACY rows 50, 51, 52 (#363) are those of `dev-swift`, this lot's row is 54 (53 left to the branch that holds it), and the spec's three mentions (l.74, 76, 78) say 54; HFR-PROTOCOL §6c keeps `### LOT-053 — smiley search and wiki` (l.459) and `### LOT-050 — moderator alert` follows (l.466). The only other change the merge made to the lot's files is the one-line call swap in `submit` and the row renumbering in the spec.\n- No line over 140 in the changed Swift files.\n- Security verdict unchanged since 6b62bd2e: POST only to an action parsing to the same target as the link, redirects not followed, sent once, no success claimed, no token or cookie in any error.\n",
